/*
  Localizable.strings (Brazilian Portuguese, pt-BR)
  CommandH

  Keys are the English source strings. SwiftUI literals (Text, Button, ...)
  and String(localized:) look them up in Bundle.main. %@ is a string argument.

  Do not translate: CommandH, Matt Senter, Senternet, Senternet LLC, other app
  names (Despacer, Weatherling, Burly, Comoji, Premail, Highwire, StockCar,
  Orgabot, BeeReady, SeedMatrix), Claude Code, Codex, Slack, :emoji:, Cmd+H,
  Cmd+Tab, or keyboard glyphs such as ⌘. Never use an em dash in a translation.

  When a string names a macOS feature or place (Dock, menu bar, Show Desktop,
  Applications folder, login), use Apple's official localized name for it.

  The Hiding pane, the sidebar, the window title and the menu bar menu appear
  in the App Store screenshots: never add the words Mac or macOS to them.

  Every key here must exist in every other .lproj, and every string the app
  shows must be a key here: scripts/check-localization.py enforces both.
*/

/* ===== Menus and window title (main.swift) ===== */

/* Settings window title. */
"CommandH Preferences" = "Ajustes do CommandH";

/* Menu item that opens the settings window (app menu and menu bar menu). */
"Preferences…" = "Ajustes…";

/* App menu item (Cmd+H). */
"Hide CommandH" = "Ocultar CommandH";

/* App menu item (Cmd+W). */
"Close Window" = "Fechar Janela";

/* App menu item on Cmd+Q: closes the window but CommandH keeps running. */
"Close and Keep Running" = "Fechar e Manter em Execução";

/* Menu item and settings button that really quits the app. */
"Quit CommandH" = "Encerrar CommandH";

/* Menu bar menu checkbox and settings switch that turns CommandH on or off. */
"Enabled" = "Ativado";

/* Menu bar submenu title for choosing how the last app is handled. */
"When Cmd+H Can't Hide" = "Quando o Cmd+H Não Puder Ocultar";

/* Menu bar submenu choice: hide the last app; CommandH briefly shows a Dock icon. */
"Hide the App (Dock icon appears)" = "Ocultar o App (ícone aparece no Dock)";

/* Menu bar submenu choice: use the system's Show Desktop instead. Show Desktop is the macOS feature name; use its official localized name. */
"Show Desktop (no Dock icon)" = "Mostrar Mesa (sem ícone no Dock)";

/* Menu bar menu checkbox that shows or hides the menu bar icon. Title case, like the other menu items. */
"Show in Menu Bar" = "Mostrar na Barra de Menus";

/* Menu bar menu checkbox that starts CommandH at login. Title case, like the other menu items. */
"Open at Login" = "Abrir ao Iniciar Sessão";

/* ===== Settings sidebar (SettingsView.swift) ===== */

/* Settings sidebar tab and pane title. */
"Hiding" = "Ocultar";

/* Settings sidebar tab and pane title. Also the label of the system version row in About. */
"System" = "Sistema";

/* Settings sidebar tab and pane title. */
"Privacy" = "Privacidade";

/* Settings sidebar tab and pane title listing the developer's other apps. */
"Other Projects" = "Outros projetos";

/* Settings sidebar tab and pane title. */
"About" = "Sobre";

/* Credit line in the sidebar and About. %@ is the developer's name, Matt Senter, which links to his site; place it where the language needs it. */
